{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-ib:000024:note_appended:bob-cli-ib.1:6be0f147de89ca6ccce45d5c82a553e5fc8c1cdf67d5f4364c53b53972ce336a","timestamp":"2026-11-07T18:03:34Z","actor":"bob-cli-ib.1","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-ib.1","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Handoff for sync/remote: partials are cron-validate (cron), cron-machine (hostname, cron), cron-block (machine, cron), cron-retire (machine, cron), plus cron-host (output=block|retire, hostname, cron) which the run_onchange hook can call twice for this host. Every partial validates first, even for unknown hosts. Gotcha: chezmoi v2.74.0 drops the middle segment of fail messages shaped \"a: <word>: c\" (prints \"a: c\"), so keep fail text to one \"path: message\" prefix. Renders are byte-identical on v2.13.1 and v2.74.0."}}
